-year-old student con-)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.18449 Tw 1.2778 TL T*(tribute to the student\325s social identity? Knowing that the student is\ a)Tj0.0141 Tc -0.0143 Tw T*(working-class African-American girl, and that the teacher is a middle-cl\ass)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.1292 Tw T*(European-American man, we might construe this as a powerful teacher)Tj0.0006 Tc -0.0007 Tw T*(silencing a disempowered student. Widely circulating categories of ident\ity,)Tj0.0076 Tc -0.0078 Tw T*(like \324working class\325 and \324African American\325 are in fact cruc\ial resources that)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.0224 Tw T*(people use, and that operate through people, as they identify themselves\)Tj0.1619 Tw T*(and others. This fragment could, of course, be uncharacteristic for the)Tj0.0507 Tw T*(teacher and the student, and there could be mitigating circumstances. If\)Tj0.1369 Tw T*(this sort of event recurred, however, we could plausibly argue that the)Tj0.0002 Tc -0.00031 Tw T*(student is being identi\336ed as \324bad\325 because this \336ts with a \widely circulating)Tj0.00211 Tc -0.0022 Tw T*(model of identity that includes \324resistant,\325 \324disruptive\325 st\udents who are dis-)Tj0.0056 Tc -0.0058 Tw T*(proportionately African American and working class.)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.06931 Tw 1 -1.2778 Td(As important as widely circulating categories of identity are, however,)Tj0.0029 Tc -0.00301 Tw -1 -1.2778 Td(many have warned that we cannot assume events like this simply represent\)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.08459 Tw T*(instances of such categories \(Gar\336nkel, 1967; Goffman, 1976; Rampton\,)Tj0.0697 Tw T*(1999; Schegloff, 1988\). Identi\336cation happens only in practice, and \it is)Tj0.0312 Tw T*(always constructed for particular purposes and in particular events. Thu\s)Tj0.007 Tc -0.0071 Tw T*(signs of identity can be interpreted only with respect to particular con\texts)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.0517 Tw T*(of use. The case above could in fact be teasing or irony, and the studen\t)Tj0.05209 Tw T*(might understand perfectly well that the teacher does not mean to label)Tj0.0088 Tc -0.0089 Tw T*(her as resistant and disruptive. In order to tell what sort of identi\336\cation is)Tj/F5 1 Tf 0.0051 Tc 0 Tw 8.5 0 0 8.5 278.4565 125.9819 Tm(\025\003\026)TjET1 g/R13 gs 91 727 222 -12 ref*BT0 g/R9 gs /F-1 1 Tf -0.01669 Tc -0.1666 Tw 8 0 0 8 93 717 Tm(12IDTR_ch10\(203-228\)  7/12/07  11:29 AM  Page 205)TjET1 G0.5 w /R13 gs 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS0 G0.25 w 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS1 G0.5 w 261.5 714 m309.5 714 l261.5 66 m309.5 66 l72 414 m72 366 l499 414 m499 366 l285.5 726 m285.5 702 l285.5 78 m285.5 54 l60 390 m84 390 l487 390 m511 390 l285.5 714 m291.5 714 l291.5 710.688 288.812 708 285.5 708 c282.188 708 279.5 710.688 279.5 714 c279.5 717.312 282.188 720 285.5 720 c288.812 720 291.5 717.312 291.5 714 c285.5 66 m291.5 66 l291.5 62.688 288.812 60 285.5 60 c282.188 60 279.5 62.688 279.5 66 c279.5 69.312 282.188 72 285.5 72 c288.812 72 291.5 69.312 291.5 66 c72 390 m78 390 l78 386.688 75.312 384 72 384 c68.688 384 66 386.688 66 390 c66 393.312 68.688 396 72 396 c75.312 396 78 393.312 78 390 c499 390 m505 390 l505 386.688 502.312 384 499 384 c495.688 384 493 386.688 493 390 c493 393.312 495.688 396 499 396 c502.312 396 505 393.312 505 390 cS0 G0.25 w 261.5 714 m309.5 714 l261.5 66 m309.5 66 l72 414 m72 366 l499 414 m499 366 l285.5 726 m285.5 702 l285.5 78 m285.5 54 l60 390 m84 390 l487 390 m511 390 l285.5 714 m291.5 714 l291.5 710.688 288.812 708 285.5 708 c282.188 708 279.5 710.688 279.5 714 c279.5 717.312 282.188 720 285.5 720 c288.812 720 291.5 717.312 291.5 714 c285.5 66 m291.5 66 l291.5 62.688 288.812 60 285.5 60 c282.