two reasons. First, Mrs Bailey believed what she said \320 she both expl\icitly)Tj-0.0119 Tw T*(and implicitly stated it throughout the year, and the girls often remind\ed)Tj0.00079 Tw T*(the boys about these alleged gender differences. Second, the boys tried \to)Tj0.0977 Tw T*(sit together in the back of the room, and all but one of them generally)Tj0.1496 Tw T*(refused to participate in class discussion, while many girls participate\d)Tj0.032 Tw T*(actively and dominated classroom discussions. For more evidence of this)Tj0.0056 Tc -0.00571 Tw T*(local gender difference, see Wortham \(2005\).)Tj/F5 1 Tf 0.0051 Tc 0 Tw 8.5 0 0 8.5 127.181 662.2017 Tm(\025\002\025)Tj/F7 1 Tf 0.005 Tc 2.4031 0 Td[(\013\f\r\001)5.1(\007\004\016\017\001)5.1(\006\020\001)5.1(\021\005\022\f\b\017\003\004\005\022\023\005\024\001)5.1(\025\022\f\005\003\023\003\016\026\025\022\f\005\003\023\003\023\f\017)]TJET1 g/R13 gs 91 727 222 -12 ref*BT0 g/R20 gs /F-1 1 Tf -0.01669 Tc -0.1666 Tw 8 0 0 8 93 717 Tm(12IDTR_ch10\(203-228\)  7/12/07  11:29 AM  Page 212)TjET1 G0.5 w 10 M 0 j 0 J []0 d /R13 gs 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS0 G0.25 w 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS1 G0.5 w 261.5 714 m309.5 714 l261.5 66 m309.5 66 l72 414 m72 366 l499 414 m499 366 l285.5 726 m285.5 702 l285.5 78 m285.5 54 l60 390 m84 390 l487 390 m511 390 l285.5 714 m291.5 714 l291.5 710.688 288.812 708 285.5 708 c282.188 708 279.5 710.688 279.5 714 c279.5 717.312 282.188 720 285.5 720 c288.812 720 291.5 717.312 291.5 714 c285.5 66 m291.5 66 l291.5 62.688 288.812 60 285.5 60 c282.188 60 279.5 62.688 279.5 66 c279.5 69.312 282.188 72 285.5 72 c288.812 72 291.5 69.312 291.5 66 c72 390 m78 390 l78 386.688 75.312 384 72 384 c68.688 384 6