 Tc -0.0125 Tw T*(African Americans relate to mainstream institutions like school, and oth\er)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.0925 Tw T*(widely circulating models and processes were relevant to Tyisha\325s soc\ial)Tj0.0157 Tc -0.01579 Tw T*(identi\336cation in this classroom. But these more widely circulating mo\dels)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.06149 Tw T*(are not suf\336cient to account for her shifts in identity, because the \shifts)Tj0.0209 Tw T*(were mediated through more local categories. Tyisha became a particular)Tj0.0331 Tw T*(type of girl, one who violated the local stereotype of promising girls a\nd)Tj0.004 Tc -0.0041 Tw T*(unpromising boys, as teachers and students borrowed categories of identi\ty)Tj0.01131 Tc -0.0114 Tw T*(from the local curricular themes. If the curriculum has not been organiz\ed)Tj0.0013 Tc -0.0014 Tw T*(as it was in this particular classroom, Tyisha\325s identity would proba\bly have)Tj0.01711 Tc 0.14819 Tw T*(developed somewhat differently. She might have been \324disruptive,\325 \but)Tj0.0522 Tw T*(probably not a \324disruptive outcast\325. In addition to the importance\ of the)Tj0.0162 Tc -0.0163 Tw T*(local timescale, the contingent shapes of particular events also in\337u\enced)Tj0 Tc -0.00011 Tw T*(how Tyisha was identi\336ed in context. But neither were her shifts in i\dentity)Tj0.0056 Tc -0.00571 Tw T*(constructed entirely at the event-level. )Tj0.0343 Tc 0.08791 Tw 1 -1.2778 Td(The analyses show how local, intermediate-timescale processes, like)Tj0.0244 Tc -0.00729 Tw -1 -1.2778 Td(the development of categories within a particular classroom over several\)Tj0.0145 Tc -0.0146 Tw T*(months, can play an essential role in constituting the social identi\336\cation)Tj0.0343 Tc -0.0096 Tw T*(of students. These processes draw on longer-timescale processes, which)Tj0.0262 Tc -0.00909 Tw T*(supply widely circulating models of identity. They also draw on shorter-\)Tj0.02 Tc -0.0029 Tw T*(timescale processes like interactional events in the classroom. But loca\lly)Tj0.0343 Tc 0.0834 Tw T*(emerging models and resources, like the curricular models of identity)Tj0.20151 Tw T*(and the habitual positions that other students took with respect to)Tj0.0271 Tc -0.00999 Tw T*(Tyisha, played an essential role in this case. In at least some cases, t\hen,)Tj0.0343 Tc 0.15041 Tw T*(we must go beyond \324macro\325 and \324micro\325 and examine other rele\vant)Tj0.0228 Tc 0 Tw T*(timescales.)Tj/F7 1 Tf 0.005 Tc 8.5 0 0 8.5 305.9225 662.2017 Tm[(\002\t\023\020\003\023\005\024\001)5.1(\025\022\f\005\003\023\003\023\f\017\001)5.2(\023\005\001)5.2(\003\t\f\001)5.2(\027\030\004\017\017\b\006\006\n)]TJ/F5 1 Tf 0.0051 Tc 14.6835 0 Td(\025\025\026)TjET1 g/R13 gs 91 727 222 -12 ref*BT0 g/R70 gs /F-1 1 Tf -0.01669 Tc -0.1666 Tw 8 0 0 8 93 717 Tm(12IDTR_ch10\(203-228\)  7/12/07  11:29 AM  Page 225)TjET1 G0.5 w 10 M 0 j 0 J []0 d /R13 gs 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS0 G0.25 w 90 726 m90 702 l60 696 m84 696 l481 726 m481 702 l511 696 m487 696 l90 54 m90 78 l60 84 m84 84 l481 54 m481 78 l511 84 m487 84 lS1 G0.5 w 261.5 714 m309.5 714 l261.5 66 m309.5 66 l72 414 m72 366 l499 414 m499 366 l285.5 726 m285.5 702 l285.5 78 m285.5 54 l60 390 m84 390 l487 390 m511 390 l285.5 714 m291.5 714 l291.5 710.688 288.812 708 285.5 708 c282.188 708 279.5 710.688 279.5 714 c279.5 717.312 282.188 720 285.5 720 c288.812 720 291.5 717.312 291.5 714 c285.5 66 m291.5 66 l291.5 62.688 288.812 60 285.5 60 c282.188 60 279.5 62.688 279.5 66 c279.5 69.312 282.188 72 285.5 72 c288.812 72 291.5 69.312 291.5 66 c72 390 m78 390 l78 386.688 75.312 384 72 384 c68.688 384 66 386.688 66 390 c66 393.312 68.688 396 72 396 c75.312 396 78 393.312 78 390 c499 390 m505 390 l505 386.688 502.312 384 499 384 c495.688 384 493 386.688 493 390 c4